I downloaded it and used it on my pathetically small logfile, and
I thought it was fun.
I have just one remark: it does not seem to be compatble with the
logmoves patch, which stores the number of moves of games in the
logfile
(this patch is available on
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html).
The number of moves is added between curly brackets at the end
of the line, and this leads to the apparition of monsters such as
"Mumak {13640}" in the top monsters list.

I don't know if it's worth to modify your script for that however, or
even if you'd care to do it ;)

The conclusion I come to with this analysis of my logfile is I should
play more games!

